counterfactuals.output:
Recent amplitude analyses have targeted penguin-dominated, charmless vector–vector modes such as

- \(B_s^0\to K^{*0}\bar K^{*0}\), with \(f_L\simeq0.20\);
- \(B_s^0\to\phi\phi\), with \(f_L\simeq0.35\);
- \(B^0\to\rho^0K^{*0}\), with \(f_L\simeq0.16\);
- and the rarer \(B^0\to K^{*0}\bar K^{*0}\), for which the measured longitudinal component is larger, roughly \(0.7\).

Thus, several rare penguin-dominated \(B\to VV\) decays are predominantly transversely polarized. Their longitudinal fractions are well below the naive heavy-quark expectation \(f_L\approx1\), reinforcing the long-standing “polarization puzzle,” although the effect is clearly mode dependent.
